{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793027135,"nonce":"SoeX4vKP1zkMrus2IKIrMDwEIIA=","message":"Implemented in 9a5ff56 (Persist hosted Save checkpoints for compute recovery).\n\nNative session:\n- hello advertises checkpoints=1. doc.save with checkpoint:true captures text and the complete Yrs state under the same read transaction, flushes that snapshot and returns a versioned SHA-256 checkpoint. Ordinary Save/flush stays compatible.\n- A reusable Rust codec checks size, version, hash, decoding and missing dependencies. Same-generation snapshots merge without reviving deleted text; incompatible causal histories fail instead of mixing graphs. Helper documents are released before the next graph is materialized.\n- doc.restore requires write authorization, a contained file path and a valid complete checkpoint. It refuses an already-materialized document and restores the graph plus text for released or absent files. Browser-forwarded restore is denied by the gateway.\n\nDurable Object:\n- Hosted Save forces native checkpoint capture and returns success only after the durable record commits. The browser receives an ID/hash receipt rather than the full snapshot. A checkpoint failure is a Save failure even if compute already wrote the file; quota reasons are preserved in the message.\n- Storage is scoped by workspace object, relative path and native recovery generation. Chunk payloads, versioned manifest and quota index are published in one atomic bulk storage operation. Obsolete chunk payloads are cleared on replacement. The SDK bulk API needs a plain object with own string properties; using a Rust map's default ES Map serialization silently wrote no keys, which the read-after-ack integration test detected. The implementation now builds the proper object explicitly.\n- Prototype bounds: 4 MiB encoded state per record, 512 records, 64 MiB raw state payload per workspace. This does not define account/tier pricing or Cloud Sync bucket limits. Native Save payloads are serialized per workspace; up to 256 small requests can queue, with admission released on cancellation and bounded queue/response deadlines. Large original request bodies are dropped before queueing.\n- Internal /checkpoints, /checkpoint and /checkpoint/import operations support the trusted control plane. They have workspace-owner guards and are not public Worker routes. Generation separation and the existing browser reconnect fence remain intact.\n\nValidation:\n- 41 native tests and a core-only build passed. New tests cover Unicode round-trip into fresh compute, no duplicated baseline, continued CRDT edits after restore, active-document refusal, write authorization, containment, checksum corruption, incomplete updates, oversized snapshots, reversed saves/deletions and incompatible histories.\n- All 9 Rust Worker tests passed. The new real-server test reads storage immediately after Save acknowledgement, queues 65 saves, replaces/shrinks chunked state, replays older snapshots without rolling back deletions, rejects corrupt imports, checks cross-owner/public-route denial, destroys compute files/state and restarts the object, restores into fresh compute, and preserves generation isolation. Record and aggregate-byte limit failures retain prior data; a hosted Save cannot falsely confirm durability on quota failure.\n- All 37 browser-session tests passed. Two full WASM editors passed collaboration, undo, Save interruption, restart/reload, tab lifecycle, context fencing and the actual recovery-preserving toast reopen action.\n- The full WASM GitHub/repository flow passed through the local Rust Worker: hosted editing, a durable receipt from Save, matching internal object read-back, and reload without reprovisioning or changed file contents. GitHub/provisioning remain mocks. The fixture now waits for the native listening socket rather than sleeping for startup; initial upgrade failures were a test readiness race. Fixture text avoids auto-indentation when testing exact storage bytes.\n\nRebuilt WASM and native session; tested app bundle staged at bin/web/rayde. Local session restarted at 127.0.0.1:7070 preserving URL/credentials/workspace/environment. Read-only live checks confirm checkpoint capability, workspace access and matching served adapter. WASM 6bd50e26d6c630fa113e6119418ad2a7afd6b4e1059c8865d3e6e0201d5b7d45; adapter 51df1406f7e3ad6bdf098d183883602c3116659358d8b5cda48aa25f52b2ac79. No production cloud deployment, push, GitHub App provisioning or real MSB provider was performed.\n\nScope boundary: explicit Save checkpoints only. Unsaved-update journaling/acknowledgement durability, whole-filesystem/tombstone materialization, automatic VM restore, leases/fencing, stable document identity, retention/cleanup, hibernation and production MSB provisioning remain open. The running direct local session is not implicitly a hosted Durable Object session.","files":null}]}